Prepare a prototype for a colleague to evaluate — learner brief
Fictional Northstar Services training material.
Handoff
Use own prototype or supplied calculator starter. Six tests: normal,boundary,invalid,reset/recovery,keyboard,reopen. README, expected/actual, defect/retest, owner and limits. No deployment.
Task
Northstar's controller wants a reviewable local prototype and evidence before considering any further development.
Actions
	1	Choose one tool and write run instructions someone can follow without the chat.
	2	Start from a clean state and execute all six required tests, recording actual results.
	3	Ask AI to inspect one failure or weakness and propose a minimal fix.
	4	Apply an understood fix and rerun affected and core cases; if no defect is found, test an additional edge case rather than fabricate one.
	5	Write known limits, including local-only use, synthetic data, untested production controls, and any accessibility gaps.
	6	Package the handoff as source and Markdown evidence only in the future learner exercise; do not publish the prototype.
Output
README content; source version; six-case expected/actual matrix; defect log; correction/retest; known limits; proposed maintenance owner role.
Supplied local practice files
	•	calculator-starter.html
Keep these files together. Scripts take explicit paths; choose new output folders. Use a plain text editor to inspect source before running. Browser prototypes open locally; do not deploy them.
